accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  finaltype  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  09 aug 94 accessioned on  09 aug 94 at 13 16 clinical data  38 year old female with cancer of left breast  status post chemotherapy with regression of tumor  now for mastectomy  please do receptors on any residual tumor                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast  left   infiltrating ductal carcinoma  grade removed_date  widespread  with extensive lymphatic invasion  removed_date lymph nodes are involved by microscopic foci of carcinoma surgical margins negative for carcinoma  additional axillary tissue  left breast   metastatic adenocarcinoma within lymphatics and one lymph node  diagnosis by  james f  southern  m d  signed on  24 aug 94 at 14 47                                                                                     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  left   the tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone