 failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  24 removed_month 93 at 13 48 gross description  received fresh   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number and  right breast re excision  is a 7 x 5 x 2cm right lumpectomy specimen with a removed_date x 0 4cm horizontal skin ellipse  a 2 2cm well healed longitudinal central scar is present within the skin ellipse  the specimen is oriented by a long stitch laterally  and a short stitch superiorly  the semifirm  yellow  fibrofatty tissue is inked yellow  laterally  and black medially  specimen is serially sectioned  revealing fibrofatty breast tissue with a removed_date x removed_date x 0 2cm white  firm area  grossly abutting the anterior  medially  black inked margin  located within the superior and inferior aspects of the sample are two biopsy cavities measuring removed_date x removed_date x 0 3cm  and removed_date x removed_date x 0 2cm  respectively  section code a b   closest margins of tumor  mid anterior medial c d   representative sections of lateral breast with skin e   representative section of medial breast with biopsy cavity f   representative section of medial breast g   repres