accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  06 removed_month 93 accessioned on  06 removed_month 93 at 14 39 clinical data   none provided                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast biopsy  right spiculated mass   intraductal carcinoma  50   and infiltrating ductal carcinoma  poorly differentiated  grade removed_date  50    with focal perineural involvement by tumor  and with tumor focally at the inked margin of the specimen  note  no vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  breast  right lateral inferior   fibrocystic change with focally atypical ductal hyperplasia  breast  right deep   fibrocystic change with atypical lobular hyperplasia   right  biopsy   brdu uptake  percentage of cells in s phase   4   see note  note  the breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating dna  positive cells  cells in s phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  results from 463 mgh cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in s phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    added by  ann d  thor  m d  signed on  23 removed_month 93 at 16 15     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of frozen tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  right spiculated mass   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  16 removed_month 93 at 14 23 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name and unit number  in three parts  labeled  right breast  is a removed_date x removed_date x 2 5cm portion of fatty breast tissue with a black suture at one end  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm hard nodule that is present 1 5cm from the suture and which focally approaches close to the margin  a portion is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  representative sections of the mass and the resection margin are submitted in u  v  and w  labeled  right breast lateral inferior  are two pieces of breast tissue  removed_date x removed_date x 2 0cm and removed_date x removed_date x 0 7cm  both are inked and sectioned to reveal fibrofatty tissue  representative sections are submitted in x y z and cc  received in formalin   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name and unit number  and  deep right breast  is a removed_date x removed_date x 0 5cm portion of fibrofatty tissue  the specimen is inked and sectioned  it is submitted entirely in aa and bb  gross description by  david weissmann  m d  resident  timothy r  quinn  md    